# TG-03 smoke test (make smoke-tgd): tgd inside Zoraya under HVF, with no account and no
# traffic to Telegram: the start, the line protocol, a clean quit, the refusal without +net,
# TDLib's database opened, written and reopened (a placeholder api id, no +net), and the
# credentials kept across a restart. Run on the volume of make root.
! panicked
! first process ended
! Traceback
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
> mkdir tg\r
< \r\n~>
> tgd --version\r
< tgd 0.1.0
< \r\n~>
# What the line of the report grants (the DC ranges, OpenRouter, ~/tg).
> grants +net 149.154.160.0/20:443 +net openrouter.ai:443 +w ~/tg tgd\r
< \r\n~>
# The refusal: no +net, so connecting to a data centre is refused (EACCES), and tgd says
# which line starts it.
> tgd --json\r
< "ev": "refused", "reason": "network"
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< exit status 3
< \r\n~>
# TDLib's database, twice: opened, written, closed; opened again.
> +w ~/tg python3 tdjson_db.py /home/tg/dbcheck\r
< run first
< state authorizationStateWaitPhoneNumber
< db done
< \r\n~>
> +w ~/tg python3 tdjson_db.py /home/tg/dbcheck\r
< run again
< state authorizationStateWaitPhoneNumber
< db done
< \r\n~>
# The protocol, without network (--no-probe): hello, a reply, an error reply, credentials
# (placeholders) that start TDLib to wait_phone, a clean quit.
> +w ~/tg tgd --json --no-probe --test-dc\r
< "ev": "hello"
< "state": "need_credentials"
> {"op": "version", "id": 1}\r
< "re": 1, "ok": true
> {"op": "nonsense", "id": 2}\r
< "re": 2, "ok": false
> {"op": "auth.credentials", "id": 3, "api_id": 1, "api_hash": "00000000000000000000000000000000"}\r
< "re": 3, "ok": true
< "state": "wait_phone"
> {"op": "quit", "id": 4}\r
< "ev": "bye"
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< succeeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
# Started again: the credentials and the database are found, TDLib asks for the phone.
> +w ~/tg tgd --json --no-probe --test-dc\r
< "ev": "hello"
< "state": "wait_phone"
> {"op": "quit", "id": 1}\r
< "ev": "bye"
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< succeeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
x power off
> poweroff\r
